# one symbol for the instantiation that owns something and none for the one that does not, out of a single
# template. the mangled owner segment carries the type arguments, so the two could never have collided - what
# this pins is that the answer is written per instance rather than once on `Box<T>`, where the first
# instantiation to be torn down would have decided it for every other
--- OUT --->
1
1
balanced
--- IR --->
# `Box<array<int32>>` owns its item, so it has a teardown, and the element type is in the symbol
CHECK: define linkonce_odr void @"_M3BoxIMLC5arrayIMLPiEE_$deinit

# and `Box<int32>` owes nothing, so nothing was written for it. the `I..E` between the owner segment and
# `_$deinit` is where its argument would be
CHECK-NOT: @"_M3BoxIMLPiE_$deinit
